{
  "title": "Synovial Sarcoma",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pathology/8052/synovial-sarcoma",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Apr 5 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Synovial Sarcoma is a malignant, soft tissue sarcoma caused by a t(X;18) chromosomal translocation mutation ( SS18:SSX fusion protein) most commonly found near joints but rarely within the joint.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The condition usually presents in patients between 15 and 40 years old with a growing mass in proximity to a joint.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with a biopsy showing a classic mono/biphasic appearance with atypical spindle cells and epithelial cells. Immunostaining is positive for epithelial membrane antigen and vimentin.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually wide surgical excision with perioperative radiation.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "5-10% of all soft tissue sarcomas",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "most common sarcoma found in adolescent age group",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "affects males and females almost equally (1.2 to 1)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "More common in the lower limbs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most commonly around the knee - popliteal fossa",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "it is the **most common sarcoma of the foot**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Mechanism",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mesenchymal soft tissue sarcoma with unknown cellular origin",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "synovial sarcoma is a misnomer due to the tumor's microscopic resemblance to mature synovium",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "synovial sarcoma typically shows high histologic grade",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "metastasis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "metastasis may develop in 30-60% of patients",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**like other sarcomas, the lung** is most common site of metastasis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "synovial sarcoma has been shown to have similar rates of lymph node metastasis compared to other soft tissue sarcomas",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "i.e angiosarcoma, clear cell sarcoma, rhabdomyosarcoma, epithelioid sarcoma",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "can stage with lymph node biopsy - called sentinel lymph node biopsy",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "while lymph node metastasis is a poor prognostic sign, it is not as bad as lung metastasis",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "4",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "metastasis is more common with large, deep, and high grade sarcomas",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Genetics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**chromosomal translocation t(X;18)** is observed in more than 90% of cases",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "translocation forms the SYT-SSX1, 2, or 4 fusion protein",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "SYT-SSX4 is rare",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "fusion proteins bind to BAF complex, which displaces the tumor suppressor BAF47",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "new BAF complex activates Sox2, which leads to tumor formation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "",
          "table": [
            {
              "header": true,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 4,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "**SYT-SSX1 vs. SYT-SSX2**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "SYT-SSX1",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "SYT-SSX2",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Frequency",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "More common (60% of tumors)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Less common (40% of tumors)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Histology type",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Biphasic (contains both spindle cells and epithelial cells)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Monophasic (contains either spindle cells OR epithelial cells)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Gender",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "M:F = 1:1",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "M:F = 1:2",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Presentation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Larger, with metastases",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Smaller, without metastases",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Survival",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Worse",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Better",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "typically present as a slow **growing mass in proximity to a joint**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "may be painless or painful",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "most commonly occur in periarticular locations",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "knee, shoulder, elbow, foot",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "60% are found in the lower extremity",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "check for **regional lymphadenopathy**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Ultrasound",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "nonspecific heterogenous hypoechoic mass",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**can show soft tissue mineralization (calcification)** in these tumors",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8052/images/Case%20B%20-%20axilla%20-%20xray%20-%20parsons_moved.jpg",
                  "caption": "extra skeletal soft tissue mass"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "may resemble heterotopic ossification",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Well circumscribed mass",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "can show calcification in the soft tissue mass",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8052/images/Case%20A%20-%20pelvis%20-%20CT%20-%20parsons_moved.png",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "CT chest for staging",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Gold standard for diagnostic imaging",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "MRI reveals a heterogenous mass that is typically dark on T1 weighted images and bright on T2 weighted images",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "T2 \"triple sign\"",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "areas of high signaling form necrosis/cystic degeneration and low signaling from calcifications and fibrosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Staging",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Biopsy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "core-needle versus incisional biopsy",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "FNA is not gold-standard as it does not provide information on tumor structure",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "CT Chest",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "PET/CT Scan",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Histology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Characteristic findings",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "classical synovial sarcoma shows a mono/biphasic appearance with two typical cell types",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**spindle cell type is most common**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "relatively small and uniform and found in sheets of malignant appearing cells with minimal cytoplasm and dark atypical nuclei",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**epithelial cell type**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "gland, nest, or cyst-like cells",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8052/images/Histology%20C%20-%20parsons_moved.jpg",
                          "caption": ""
                        },
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8052/images/Histology%20B%20-%20Parsons_moved.png",
                          "caption": "typical histologic appearance"
                        },
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8052/images/Histology%20A_moved.jpg",
                          "caption": ""
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "cellular origin of synovial sarcoma is unknown",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Immunostaining",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "synovial sarcoma stains positive for",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**vimentin**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**epithelial membrane antigen**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "sporadic S-100",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "epithelial cells stain positive for **keratin**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "wide surgical resection with perioperative radiotherapy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "standard of care in most patients",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "radiotherapy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "may be delivered in neoadjuvant or adjuvant fashion",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "no consensus as to which provides better outcomes",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "decreases the rate of local recurrence and improves overall survival and disease-specific survival",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "chemotherapy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "data regarding chemotherapy in synovial sarcoma suggests that chemotherapy may improve both local control and overall survival",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "routine use is limited and there is no consensus for regimen or timing of chemotherapy",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "Reserved for high risk tumors, metastatic disease, and younger populations",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Overall prognosis is poor",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
